<s-1 id="RM000000IVP01BX_02_0021" proc-id="RM0550J___0000ABI00000">
<ptxt>Inspect Compressor Assembly (w/ Pulley) Operation (Engine Type 2AZ-FE)</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Put a mark on the compressor assembly (with pulley) at the position shown in the illustration.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E144442J01" width="7.106578999in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Start the engine and check that the mark on the compressor assembly (with pulley) rotates together with the pulley.</ptxt>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM000000IVP01BX_02_0023" proc-id="RM0550J___0000ABK00000">
<ptxt>Inspect Cooler Condenser Assembly</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>If the fins of the cooler condenser assembly are dirty, clean them with water and dry them with compressed air.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Do not damage the fins of the cooler condenser assembly.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>If the fins of the cooler condenser assembly are bent, straighten them with a screwdriver or pliers.  </ptxt>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM000000IVP01BX_02_0024" proc-id="RM0550J___0000ABL00000">
<ptxt>Inspect for Refrigerant Leaks</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Using a halogen leak detector, check the piping joints for gas leaks.</ptxt>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>If there is a gas leak at a piping joint, check the torque of the joint. </ptxt>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
